the copyright holders are entitled to grant.

2. Permitted use

Subject to this license, permission is granted to use, reproduce, modify and
redistribute the Materials and modifications of them solely for non-commercial
academic research and education. Commercial use and use for other purposes
require prior written permission from the copyright holders. Permission
requests can be sent to e.r.salcedoaliaga@qmul.ac.uk.

3. Required citation and notices

Every reuse of the Materials or modifications of them must acknowledge the
BLPR project and cite the following paper:

  Auza Banegas, G. J., Calvimontes Vera, D. A., Condori Peredo, N. L.,
  Salcedo, E., and Castro Sandoval, S. S. (2027). BLPR: Robust License Plate
  Recognition Under Viewpoint and Illumination Variations via Confidence-Driven
  VLM Fallback. In Advances in Soft Computing, MICAI 2026, Lecture Notes in
  Computer Science, vol. 17150, pp. 458-484. Springer.
  https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-032-44179-9_28

Include the citation in each publication, presentation, report, documentation,
repository, or other material that describes, incorporates, or accompanies the
reuse. If the reuse produces no such material, record the citation in the
associated research or teaching records. Redistributed copies and modifications
must retain this license, the copyright notice, and applicable attribution
notices, and must identify any modifications made.

